# Fixtures under tests/data/ are committed on purpose: the C++ suite must run without a Python
# toolchain, and the conformance fixture is the record of what XRADIO actually writes. Only the
# intermediate FITS the conformance generator writes is transient, and it deletes that itself.

AGENTS.md

# Working documents stay local. The ADRs, the design draft and the compatibility baseline are the
# record a reader of this repository needs; the rest are research drafts, a measurement log and a
# rendered atlas, none of them finished and none of them in the project's language.
docs/implementation-plan.md
docs/read-api.md
docs/sidecar.md
docs/architecture.html
docs/*.xlsx

# An unreferenced schema spreadsheet kept for reference while the XRADIO layout is still moving.
Image Data Schema.xlsx
